.TH XPS13-CAMERA-SETUP 8 "November 2026" "xps13-ubuntu-camera 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
xps13-camera-setup \- detect Dell XPS 13 camera hardware and apply model-specific fixes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xps13-camera-setup
.RB [ \-\-status | \-\-camera\-id | \-\-configure | \-\-unconfigure ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Detects the laptop model (DMI), the Intel camera unit (IPU6 or IPU7, by PCI ID) and the
OV02C10 / HM1092 sensors (ACPI), and reports or applies the parts of
.B xps13-ubuntu-camera
that depend on them. Without options it prints what was detected and installed.
.TP
.B \-\-camera\-id
Print the RGB webcam's libcamera camera ID (its ACPI path, e.g. \e_SB_.LNK1).
.TP
.B \-\-configure
(root) On IPU6 machines (XPS 13 9340), build the IPU6 boot-crash fix with DKMS if the
matching linux-source package is installed; otherwise say how to install it. Run by the
package's postinst; run it again after installing linux-source.
.TP
.B \-\-unconfigure
(root) Remove what \-\-configure added.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xps13-camera-check (1),
.BR dkms (8),
/usr/share/doc/xps13-ubuntu-camera/
